Implemented 3 custom tools for easy LLM provider configuration and switching.

NEW FILES (4):

1. setup-llm.js (150 lines) - Interactive Setup Wizard
   - Menu-driven provider selection
   - API key input with validation
   - Configuration file auto-save
   - Provider information display
   - Configuration validation
   - Manual .env editing support

   Features:
   ✅ 8 providers pre-configured
   ✅ Auto-save to .env and user-config.json
   ✅ Graceful error handling
   ✅ User-friendly prompts

   Usage:
   $ node setup-llm.js
   # Opens interactive menu

2. llm-manager.js (420 lines) - Provider Manager Library
   - Programmatic API for provider management
   - Read/write .env and config files
   - Provider validation
   - Quick switch functionality
   - Test provider connection
   - Export configuration templates

   Functions:
   - readEnv() / writeEnv() - Manage .env file
   - readConfig() / writeConfig() - Manage user-config.json
   - setProvider(id, apiKey) - Set provider + key
   - getCurrentProvider() - Get current config
   - validateProvider(id) - Validate config
   - listProviders() - List all with status
   - quickSwitch(id) - Fast provider switch
   - testProvider(id) - Test connection
   - getProviderInfo(id) - Get details
   - exportConfig(id) - Export template

   Usage:
   import { setProvider, getCurrentProvider } from './llm-manager.js';
   setProvider('groq', 'gsk-xxxxx');

3. llm-cli.js (400 lines) - Command-Line Interface
   - Fast command-line provider management
   - No wizard needed, direct commands
   - Perfect for automation & scripting

   Commands:
   - list              List all providers
   - current           Show current provider
   - switch <p>        Switch provider
   - set-key <p> <k>   Set API key
   - validate          Validate config
   - test <p>          Test connection
   - info <p>          Show provider info
   - show-env          Show .env settings
   - help              Show help

   Usage:
   $ node llm-cli.js switch groq
   $ node llm-cli.js set-key groq gsk-xxxxx
   $ node llm-cli.js validate
   $ node llm-cli.js test groq

4. LLM-CUSTOM-SETUP.md (500+ lines) - Comprehensive Documentation
   - Complete usage guide for all 3 tools
   - Quick start examples
   - Detailed command reference
   - Programmatic API examples
   - Workflow examples
   - Troubleshooting guide
   - Provider quick reference table

SUPPORTED PROVIDERS (8):

Cloud Providers:
  ✅ openrouter    - Default, multi-model (Claude, GPT, Mistral, etc.)
  ✅ openai        - GPT-4, GPT-3.5 Turbo
  ✅ anthropic     - Claude Opus, Sonnet, Haiku
